hello i'm wolfgang puck and today i'm  gonna show you how to make a delicious  mushroom risotto if you know the  technique you can do it just as well as  me  the most important part is the rice now  this is canaroli rice it comes from  northern italy which is just perfect for  risotto because it makes the risotto  really creamy let me show you how to  chop an onion you have the root here  and the stem on this side so we cut the  stem off but we leave a little bit of  the root to hold it together and then  you slice it just like i do and then one  time in half and look how easy  and another quick technique hold it with  your fingers down here  and then we chop  see that up and down  maybe you wonder what we do with garlic  i just smash it see the cloves here  like this  one two  three just go like that and you're done  when you make a stock at home it really  depends if you make a chicken stock or a  vegetable stock or a fish stock a fish  dog we only cook for 45 minutes  vegetable stock maybe for an hour  chicken or beef stock maybe for five  hours we don't throw anything away this  onion leftover which i didn't chop put  it in my stock here still get the flavor  these are three mushrooms you can find  in any store these days  so we cut off the stem  and put it in our stock this one the  same root here we're gonna cut it off  just like this and put it in our stock  see that the shiitake mushroom the stems  are really tough so in the stock they go  i love the flavor of the cheetah cape  but just the cap the best way to clean  mushrooms use a wet towel and you wipe  up  the top we have this clamshell mushrooms  and just  give the stock a lot of flavor now we're  gonna turn up the heat a little bit and  let it simmer slowly when i go to the  farmer's market if i find peas i find  asparagus or great carrots any  vegetables you like you can use for  risotto risotto is a great flavor  carrier so you can actually  use whatever you like now we have the  garlic we have the onions we're gonna  put about three tablespoon of olive oil  in our pan i have a great sous chef or  he could be a chef anywhere in any  restaurant in any hotel this is andrew  andrew is working with me how many years  ten to twelve at least we are heating up  the olive oil through the garlic  the onions  and did already some chopping for me  here i can add a little bit i don't want  to make him feel bad and hurt his  feelings it's just as good if not better  than mine  it smells already if you do that at home  and you have guests over naturally the  guests have to wait for the rice the  rice does not wait for the guests we  don't want to brown the onions just cook  them until they're glossy like i do here  and then we're gonna add the rice  we're gonna glaze the rice here with the  olive oil the onion and the garlic now  when i cook at home they'll always have  a glass of wine for me too so cheers  just use the same vinyl drink also for  your cooking you can see the rice is  perfectly glazed here a little wine  about half a cup is enough  good you can measure at home but you  know i did that a few times already in  my life even i look so young but i did  it many times i grew up eating a lot of  rice in southern austria but never  really risotto the first time a good  customer of ours wanted to have risotto  in his house i did a party and i said  okay i bring five pounds of rice and was  maybe for 20 people and i get a big pot  i started to make the risotto and you  know once you add the liquid the stock  to it it grows it grows i didn't know  what to do anymore i threw half of it  into the sink it clogged up the sink i  had my chef underneath and unclogging  the pipes of the sink to be able to cook  so when you make risotto  you don't need a lot i also like it as  an appetizer i cook the rice with the  wine until the wine is completely  evaporated the important part of the  wine is to give the food balance the  acidity of the wine gives the food  balance our stock is ready here hmm i  can smell  the freshness of the mushrooms  i'm gonna put about two ladle fulls of  stock in here and we're gonna start  cooking the risotto we add the stock a  little at the time like half a cup to a  cup at the time if you add everything at  once you're gonna have a soup and you  don't know how much you need the  stirring really helps to remove the  starch from the outside of the rice and  make your risotto nice and creamy it  takes about 20 minutes to make a risotto  so you can go from a to c in 20 minutes  as long as you have your measurements  ready what is the amazon plus to get  everything ready so all you have to do  is cook my rice is cooking along here so  i'm gonna add a little more of the stock  i have my risotto on about a medium heat  but just be sure that it cooks gently  we're gonna cook our mushrooms i always  start with olive oil first because if i  would add butter in here it might burn  it so the olive oil i'm now gonna add  maybe a tablespoon of butter here okay  and we're gonna continue adding stock to  our rice  now i'm gonna saute the mushroom you  know onion or shallots and garlic for  mushroom is perfect i always use fresh  ground pepper because it makes  everything taste so much better it has  more power it's spicier but is the aroma  of the pepper make everything smell  better and taste better my mushrooms are  pretty dry in here so what do i gonna do  i'm gonna add a little bit of my stock  it will steam it up and i can saute my  mushroom perfectly often people say oh  the risotto will cook by itself no you  have to stay next to it and steal it  constantly but it's a lot of fun you can  do it with your children at home they  learn how to make it you saute your  onion your garlic put the rice in a  little wine if you have if you don't  like wine and put a little white white  vinegar a few tablespoons that way you  have the right balance and then just  continue stirring the rice i use some  sea salt here and don't add too much at  the beginning i love pepper my risotto  is always a little peppery i always tell  people you buy the best ingredients and  then try not to screw them up so that's  so simple i'm gonna add a little more  stock  okay and i think my mushrooms are done  i'm gonna turn the fire off here i'm  gonna take about half of my mushrooms  and i'm gonna blend them by planting  some of your mushrooms will give the  risotto creaminess but also extra  flavors even if you're a vegan you make  the risotto with the mushrooms in like  that it's gonna be perfectly creamy you  don't need butter and cheese  perfect  mmm smells delicious and it [ __ ] up my  lenses too but it's good now we're gonna  add our mushroom puree here look at that  so it's totally creamy mushrooms we are  gonna taste my rice it might be on maybe  a little more  getting there  even if you have a steak a chicken  breast or some fresh meat make a  mushroom puree that's magic we stir it  constantly so that way it doesn't burn  it does not touch to the bottom also  it's important to make the risotto  really creamy let's taste one more time  i would say we are two minutes away i'm  gonna add a little more stock to it now  i'm gonna add peas to it for color but  also for taste because the peas are very  sweet i always put hot food on hot  plates it's very important you don't  want to put hot food on a cold plate the  food will get cold so you put your  plates in the oven that way they are  nice and warm we love butter and we love  parmesan cheese that makes everything  taste better butter here i'm gonna turn  the stove to low  and incorporate the butter butter fat  emulsifies the liquid even more so with  the starch so you even get more  creaminess into your risotto parmesan  very important i always buy a chunk of  parmesan and then grate it freshly into  my risotto don't buy the one which is  already grated in little plastic bags in  the supermarket because they lose use  all the leftovers they can't use  in chunks parmesan has the umami flavor  it makes everything taste better so be  generous with the parmesan we call it a  microplane it is a great grater just be  careful when you grate it maybe even use  a towel so that way you don't grate your  fingers in there i'm gonna turn off the  heat now stir in the parmesan and we're  gonna taste it one more time let's taste  it and you taste it andrew  what do you think  i think the rice is perfect it's perfect  maybe a little little all right put a  little salt  not too much because i have high blood  pressure you want to be sure when you  cook a risotto it's not like a porridge  should have just a little bite to it so  that the grains are not mushy i'm gonna  taste it how it goes with my chardonnay  here  a good rich chardonnay or a pinot is a  perfect accompaniment for your risotto  if the guests are not seated right away  be sure stop your risotto  and in case your risotto gets to take a  little bit more stock you want the  risotto bean nice and creamy my last  taste  amazing now i'm gonna show you how to  plate it we have our warm plate here  put it in the center  as much or as little as you want you  know if you just eat the risotto like  for me at home with my children with my  wife we just cooked a risotto and that's  our dinner maybe a salad on the side but  you can have a grilled chicken breast  whatever you like i remember i did the  academy award once i made a truffle  risotto and then served it with a  chicken breast look on my plate here  that is sort of consistency should be if  you move it  the risotto should be able to move so it  flattens out on our plate here see that  i have my mushrooms here  a spoonful in the center and again more  parmesan  okay we have a little fresh herbs chives  parsley whatever you like you can chop  it up sprinkle it over and we'll found  pea tenders because i have peas in here  already  so we're going to add a little peat  handle so to make it look good you know  we eat with our eyes first so it's  really important to make the  presentation really beautiful but you  don't have to do a lot you can go to the  farmer's market or to your local market  and find things like bee dandel also  edible flowers take off the petals  and then you sprinkle a few on it so now  all of a sudden it looks like spring or  summer now you know how to make the  perfect risotto just don't open a  restaurant next to spago because i won't  like you if you do that andrew what do  you think it's gorgeous chef all the  different colors but the taste is the  most important part and a few mushrooms  in your first bite  and now you know how to make a great  risotto until next time we are gonna  show you more but you also can watch my  documentary on disney plus it's called  wolfgang  [Music]  you

